## Optimal Solution

```python
class Solution:
    def reverseParentheses(self, s: str) -> str:
        n = len(s)

        openBracket = []
        door = [0] * n

        # First pass: Pair up parentheses
        for i in range(n):
            if s[i] == '(':
                openBracket.append(i)

            elif s[i] == ')':
                j = openBracket.pop()
                door[i] = j
                door[j] = i

        # Second pass: Build the result string
        result = []
        direction = 1  # Left to Right

        i = 0
        while 0 <= i < n:
            if s[i] == '(' or s[i] == ')':
                i = door[i]
                direction = -direction
            else:
                result.append(s[i])

            i += direction

        return ''.join(result)

TC: O(n)
SC: O(n)
